Rem AMOS Professional 2.00. Paste routines after End.
Hide
Palette $000,$FFF
Paper 0 : Pen 1
Cls 0
PL_COUNT=0 : PL_STEP=3 : PL_LASTSCAN=-1
Repeat
   Locate 0,0
   Print "A advances, X ignored, Q quits"
   Print "Count: ";PL_COUNT;"     "
   Gosub PL_READ_FRESH
   Gosub PL_ADVANCE
Until PL_KEY$="Q"
Show
End

Rem Globals: PL_COUNT and PL_STEP are integers from 0 to 255.
Rem PL_KEY$ is supplied by the caller; PL_ACCEPTED is the result.
Rem Only A advances; Q and other characters leave state unchanged.
PL_ADVANCE:
PL_ACCEPTED=0
If PL_KEY$="A"
   PL_COUNT=PL_COUNT+PL_STEP
   If PL_COUNT>=256
      PL_COUNT=PL_COUNT-256
   End If
   PL_ACCEPTED=1
End If
Return

Rem Initialise PL_LASTSCAN=-1 once; retain it across calls.
Rem Returns PL_KEY$ and updates PL_LASTSCAN; blocks until a fresh key.
PL_READ_FRESH:
If PL_LASTSCAN>=0
   Repeat
      Wait Vbl
   Until Key State(PL_LASTSCAN)=0
End If
Clear Key
Repeat
   PL_KEY$=Upper$(Inkey$)
   Wait Vbl
Until PL_KEY$<>""
PL_LASTSCAN=Scancode
Return
